  "headline": "Full-distribution unit-provenance audit (T4 escalation) of the NIST CORR-DATA marine steel KPI's seawater_uncoated_substrate_baselines, extending nist-baseline-descriptive-boundary-provenance-v1's 2-field row-trace to all 25 rate-valued reported fields via independent whole-array reconstruction from the mils/yr column. n=142 Seawater records, 0 missing a mils/yr entry. Of 25 rate fields compared, 4 breach the 20% bar: Aluminum and alloys/min_mm_yr=78%; Copper and alloys/min_mm_yr=86%; Nickel and alloys/max_mm_yr=59%; Stainless steels/p25_mm_yr=62%. Conclusion: H0 (the descriptive block is aggregate-unit-consistent across its full reported field surface) is H0 REFUTED.",
