  "prior_audit_relationship": "Escalation of evidence/audit/nist-baseline-descriptive-boundary-provenance-v1/ (2026-08-14, H0_REFUTED, 2/10 boundary values breached: Aluminum min 675%, Nickel max 59%). That audit traced only the single row supplying each group's min_mm_yr/max_mm_yr (2 of 30 reported fields, the only ones traceable to one row) and explicitly left the other 20 (n/p25/median/p75 x 5 groups) untested. This audit covers all 25 rate-valued fields (n excluded as a coverage diagnostic, not a rate comparison) via independent whole-array reconstruction from the mils/yr column rather than single-row tracing, so it can catch a broad unit-consistency defect that no single-row trace would surface. Does not dispute or repeat the prior finding; both breaches it names are additionally reproduced below via this whole-array method as a cross-method consistency check.",
